From: Vivek Kulkarni <vivek@redwood.ai>
To: Stephanie Nguyen <stephanie@redwood.ai>, Monica Patel <monica@redwood.ai>
Date: 2026-11-15T08:05:00-07:00
Subject: Re: Integration kickoff: Implementation notes + sample configs

Stephanie / Monica —

Following Samira's payload and concurrency notes, I've put together a minimal-run implementation checklist and concrete config snippets we should give Acme during the walkthrough. Paste this into the call notes.

1) Recommended client timeouts & retries (SDK defaults we ship):
- Connect timeout: 2s
- Request timeout (per call): 30s for sync inference; 120s for long-gen jobs
- Retry policy: exponential backoff with jitter, retries up to 3 on 5xx and 429 with increasing backoff (base 0.5s)
- 429 handling: treat as signal to throttle — if 429s exceed 1% of calls over 5m, advise immediate reduction in client-side parallel requests and enable prefix caching.

2) Sample Node snippet (from sdk-example-snippets.zip):
const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new Redwood.Client({ key: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY, timeout: 30000 });
async function call() {
  try {
    const res = await client.generate({ model: 'redwood-large-v1', messages, max_tokens: 600, retry: { retries: 3 } });
    console.log(res.output[0].content);
  } catch (e) {
    // on 429: exponential backoff and reduce concurrency
    console.error('call failed', e.message);
  }
}

3) Curl example for endpoint migration smoke test:
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.example.com/v1/generate \n  -H "Authorization: Bearer <SANDBOX_KEY>" \n  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \n  -d '{"model":"redwood-large-v1","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"..."},{"role":"user","content":"test"}],"max_tokens":100}'

4) Rate-limit guidance (initial thresholds):
- Burst window: allow up to 300 RPS for 30s while monitoring 5xx/latency.
- Steady-state: recommend starting at 75 RPS and use adaptive ramp (25% increase every 10 minutes if error rate <0.5%).

5) Cutover plan (for Acme to migrate from staging to test endpoint):
- Day 0: smoke test with 5 synthetic requests, confirm auth and telemetry.
- Day 1: ramp to 10 RPS for 1 hour; validate latency and error percent.
- Day 2: if stable, proceed to controlled load (50 RPS) with monitoring dashboards open.

I've attached the short checklist and the sample snippets to the drive link. For the walkthrough please cover: SDK install, env var setup, curl smoke tests, how to detect 429 vs other 5xx in logs, and which dashboard charts to watch (token rate, 429 rate, 5xx rate, avg latency).

Also note: we'll enable a temporary increased quota for ACME-42 in sandbox for the 11/18 window — Monica to confirm.

-Vivek
Principal Solutions Engineer, Redwood Inference

